{"id": "EUVD-2026-64392", "enisaUuid": "7d0ab03d-c5db-3186-b3c6-19bc38acfc66", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nudp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation\n\n__skb_udp_tunnel_segment() gets the UDP header before ensuring the\ntunnel header is in the skb head. If the pull reallocates skb->head,\nthe saved UDP header pointer is no longer valid.\n\nGet the UDP header after the pull to avoid a potential use-after-free.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:33:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:16:10", "baseScore": 10.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a733a38b983d8c2e222f13968209010cf44de87", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/19d89b13a43640b2da2f277ee462d919d988cb6f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b3df61bb745eb5201eac22679a2839d4ccbf3442", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ae134c012e10384cdac420b5cc6e0615cde0b55", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5161e67c561c4f28a5d9335a6e859b02511de92b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64d322c288577793eedd352b96ef75234ed380fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/588d4a6795d99d080f74ef0b5f391ea8c453ae5d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d0f86fb36eb260abd10007b62c9dcc1028e03e61"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rcm8-q4cm-988v", "CVE-2026-74705"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.5, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00364500-0041-3434-b155-44f04cf26beb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.265"}, {"id": "182b99e1-b015-3d7e-a1e4-9d2cdc0de5ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.45"}, {"id": "19491db6-305e-3093-88ff-16520fac59b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}, {"id": "30030794-2900-3437-a478-48b1c0ada9e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dbef491ebe7f3a4fb1b9111878b86a